  "projects": [
   {
    "name": "Richmond Artist Website Redesign",
    "description": "Robert Meganck is a Richmond-based artist who was in need of website redesign to simply the process of making website updates.\n\nThe core problem wasn't the aesthetics of the site but primarily that Robert couldn't maintain the site himself on Wordpress. Constant updates, technical complexity, and his own comfort level with technology was making it difficult to complete daily tasks.\n\nSquarespace has a great user-friendly interface Robert was able to use with ease. I designed the site including how to present his artwork, navigation structure, and a blog flow for him to upload new work without support. We also focused on search-ability within the site including finding artwork through keywords, songs, and musical artist. The search function is now improved, creating a better user experience. \n\nI built out tutorial videos and doing hands-on training so the handoff actually stuck. He's now updating it himself regularly.\n\nCheck out the site -> meganck.com\n\n---\n\n\"I have a new website. It’s a switch from WordPress to Squarespace. The new site is more user friendly, searchable and for those interested – easy to find which items are for sale. I couldn’t have done this without guidance from Natali Anderson, Digital Services Consultant. She has been great to work with. She addressed all my concerns and when I needed to know how to do something, so that I can do it on my own later, she would make and send me a how-to video. Thanks Natali.\"\n- Robert Meganck",
    "is_current": false
   }
