  "about": "Web development taught me systems. Client work taught me people. The overlap between those two things is where I do my best work.\n\nNow working at Virginia Commonwealth University, I contribute to the presence of the School of Medicine's multiple web properties to reach students, faculty, and the community. \n\nPreviously working as a Digital Content Manager, I handled everything from project management and client relations to end-to-end web design and development. Across industries and the full stack of creative and technical demands that come with building things people use.\n\nWhile at James Madison University, I served as Creative Director at a student-run PR firm, managing a team of creatives and driving high-impact results for internal marketing initiatives. \n\nMy toolkit covers design thinking, web development, HTML/CSS, SEO, social media management, and project management, with a strong focus on client communication. I have an eye for design and know how to apply it where it actually matters, on a technical scale.",
